// bin/claude_limits.nv — entry point of the claude-limits binary.
//
// Task T0.0 (plan 01.5) fills this with a version line only: the skeleton has to
// build, run and be testable before any real behaviour lands. Argument parsing,
// the config, the pollers, the server and the widget arrive with Ф.1–Ф.3
// (plan 01 §6); the module tree they grow into is plan 01 §3.2.
//
// `println` is called HERE and nowhere else, and that is a constraint of the
// compiler rather than a matter of taste: measured on T0.0, `println` in any
// non-entry module type-checks but fails codegen with `undefined identifier
// println` in every unit that imports it. Anything printable therefore comes in
// as a value from a pure module. Repro: docs/reports/T0.0.md.
//
// A consequence worth keeping: no test imports this file. It would pull `main` —
// and its `println` — into the test's own compilation unit, which is how the
// defect above first showed up.
//
// Module path mirrors the file path from the SOURCE ROOT: a file in a
// subdirectory carries no package prefix (`bin.claude_limits`), while a file
// directly in the root does (`claude_limits.version`). Learned from
// E_D78_MODULE_PATH_MISMATCH on T0.0; sibling packages look different only
// because they set `[lib] src = "src"`.

module bin.claude_limits

import claude_limits.version.{version_line}

fn main() {
    println(version_line())
}
